---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PlannerCTA from '../../components/PlannerCTA.astro';
import SelectSaunasButton from '../../components/SelectSaunasButton.astro';

const reviewedAt = 'August 15, 2026';

const picks = [
  {
    label: 'Lowest current cabin price',
    name: 'Dynamic Gracia 1-2 Person Low EMF FAR Infrared Sauna',
    reviewedPrice: '$1,999',
    href: 'https://selectsaunas.com/products/dynamic-saunas-dyn-6119-01-gracia-1-2-person-low-emf-far-infrared-sauna',
    fit: 'A compact indoor cabin for one regular user who wants room for an occasional second person.',
    facts: [
      'Published 1-2 person capacity',
      '39 x 36 x 75-inch exterior',
      '120V / 15A electrical service',
      'Seven carbon heating elements',
    ],
    verify: [
      'A dedicated outlet may still be the practical choice; confirm the manual and local electrical requirements.',
      'The 1-2 person label does not guarantee comfortable shoulder room for every pair of users.',
      'The retailer reports its own EMF measurement range. We have not independently tested it.',
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Lower-EMF configuration',
    name: 'Dynamic Gracia Elite 1-2 Person Ultra-Low EMF FAR Infrared Sauna',
    reviewedPrice: '$2,299',
    href: 'https://selectsaunas.com/products/dynamic-saunas-gracia-elite-1-2-person-ultra-low-emf-far-infrared-sauna',
    fit: 'A buyer who likes the Gracia footprint but wants the retailer-listed lower EMF configuration.',
    facts: [
      'Published 1-2 person capacity',
      'Natural hemlock construction',
      'Bluetooth audio and interior controls',
      'Clasp-together panel assembly',
    ],
    verify: [
      'Ask for the current model number and manual before ordering.',
      'Treat EMF figures as retailer or manufacturer claims unless you have independent measurements.',
      'Confirm final dimensions, outlet requirements, delivery access, and stock with the seller.',
    ],
  },
  {
    label: 'Full-spectrum option near the cap',
    name: 'Dynamic Gracia 1-2 Person Full Spectrum Near-Zero EMF Sauna',
    reviewedPrice: '$2,899',
    href: 'https://selectsaunas.com/products/dynamic-gracia-1-2-person-full-spectrum-near-zero-emf-far-ir-sauna-canadian-hemlock-2026-model',
    fit: 'A buyer who wants a full-spectrum configuration and is comfortable using nearly the entire $3,000 product budget.',
    facts: [
      'Published 1-2 person capacity',
      '36 x 39 x 75-inch exterior',
      '120V / 15A service with a dedicated outlet recommended by the listing',
      'Indoor use only',
    ],
    verify: [
      'The listed price leaves little room for tax, room preparation, or delivery exceptions.',
      'Confirm that the exact model and heater configuration match the listing before checkout.',
      'The retailer reports the EMF specification. We have not independently tested it.',
    ],
  },
];
---
<Base
  title="Best Saunas Under $3,000 (2026): Three Current Buyer-Fit Options"
  description="Three current indoor infrared sauna configurations listed below $3,000, with verified dimensions, electrical requirements, price caveats, and project-budget guidance."
  canonical="/guides/best-saunas-under-3000"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <header class="mb-8 max-w-3xl">
      <p class="text-sm text-amber-700 font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide mb-2">Budget Buying Guide</p>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold text-stone-900 leading-tight mb-4">
        Best Saunas Under $3,000
      </h1>
      <p class="text-stone-500 text-sm">Retailer listings reviewed {reviewedAt} · 8 min read</p>
      <p class="text-lg text-stone-600 mt-4">
        A $3,000 product budget can buy a complete indoor infrared cabin. It usually cannot cover a finished outdoor traditional-sauna project once the heater, electrical work, base, delivery, and weather protection are counted.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden mb-8">
      <img src="/images/lifestyle/barrel-sauna-field.jpg" alt="Compact outdoor barrel sauna used to illustrate a larger traditional sauna project" class="w-full object-cover max-h-80" loading="lazy" width="1200" height="800" />
    </div>

    <section class="border-y border-stone-200 py-6 mb-8" aria-labelledby="budget-reality">
      <h2 id="budget-reality" class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">What the budget buys now</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-5 text-sm text-stone-700">
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-1">Indoor infrared</p>
          <p>Several compact, plug-in cabins fit below the cap at the retailer prices we reviewed.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-1">Traditional sauna</p>
          <p>A heater or partial kit may fit. A complete installed room or outdoor structure generally needs a separate project budget.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-1">Portable steam</p>
          <p>This is a lower-cost format, but it is not an infrared cabin or a traditional sauna. Compare it separately.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <aside class="bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 rounded-lg p-5 mb-8 text-sm text-amber-950">
      <p><strong>Price rule:</strong> the figures below are retailer snapshots, not guaranteed checkout prices. Confirm stock, shipping, tax, exact model, and final price before ordering. We receive a commission if you buy through a qualifying partner link.</p>
      <p class="mt-3">Holding the product cap below $2,000? Start with the <a href="/guides/best-saunas-under-2000/" class="font-semibold underline underline-offset-2">lower-budget format guide</a> before stretching the project total.</p>
    </aside>

    <PlannerCTA
      source="best_saunas_under_3000_above_fold"
      heading="Check the room, circuit, and real project total first"
      description="Build a private planning brief before comparing listings. Your information stays in your browser unless you explicitly submit it for a manual review."
    />

    <section aria-labelledby="shortlist" class="mt-12">
      <h2 id="shortlist" class="text-3xl font-bold text-stone-900 mb-3">Three current configurations to compare</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-600 mb-8 max-w-3xl">These are not arbitrary first-, second-, and third-place rankings. Each configuration fits a different tradeoff inside the same compact indoor-cabin category.</p>

      <div class="space-y-10">
        {picks.map((pick) => (
          <section class="border-t border-stone-300 pt-7" aria-label={pick.name}>
            <div class="md:flex md:items-start md:justify-between gap-6 mb-4">
              <div>
                <p class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide text-amber-700 mb-2">{pick.label}</p>
                <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold text-stone-900">{pick.name}</h3>
              </div>
              <p class="text-sm text-stone-600 mt-2 md:mt-1 shrink-0">Listed at review: <strong class="text-stone-900">{pick.reviewedPrice}</strong></p>
            </div>

            <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5"><strong>Who it may fit:</strong> {pick.fit}</p>

            <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6 mb-5">
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Documented listing details</h4>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700">
                  {pick.facts.map((fact) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">+</span><span>{fact}</span></li>)}
                </ul>
              </div>
              <div>
                <h4 class="font-semibold text-stone-900 mb-2">Confirm before buying</h4>
                <ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-stone-700">
                  {pick.verify.map((item) => <li class="flex gap-2"><span aria-hidden="true">-</span><span>{item}</span></li>)}
                </ul>
              </div>
            </div>

            <SelectSaunasButton href={pick.href} label="Check current listing" ctaPosition="under_3000_shortlist" />
          </section>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-14 border-t border-stone-300 pt-8">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4 text-stone-900">Can an outdoor sauna stay under $3,000?</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-700 mb-4">
        A product listing can. A complete project is harder. Outdoor buyers may still need a heater, stones, a weather-ready base, a dedicated circuit or chimney system, delivery access, permits, and assembly help. A low kit price can hide those costs.
      </p>
      <p class="text-stone-700 mb-5">
        Start with the full project rather than forcing the structure into a product-only ceiling. Our <a href="/tools/sauna-cost-calculator/" class="font-semibold text-emerald-800 underline underline-offset-2">sauna cost calculator</a> separates the major line items, and the <a href="/guides/best-outdoor-sauna-of-2026/" class="font-semibold text-emerald-800 underline underline-offset-2">outdoor buyer-fit shortlist</a> covers current complete-sauna routes.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6 text-stone-900">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="divide-y divide-stone-200 border-y border-stone-200">
        <div class="py-6">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Do these prices include the whole project?</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">No. They are retailer product prices observed on the review date. Tax, room preparation, electrical work, delivery exceptions, and optional services can change the total.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-6">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Does 120V mean any outlet will work?</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">Not automatically. Confirm the exact manual, outlet type, circuit load, GFCI guidance, and local code. One of the listings specifically recommends a dedicated outlet.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-6">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Are the EMF labels independently verified?</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">Not by Backyard Sauna Pro. We report the retailer or manufacturer terminology and identify the stated measurement range when it is published. Ask the seller for the test method if that specification drives your purchase.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="py-6">
          <h3 class="font-bold text-stone-900 mb-2">Should two people assume a 1-2 person cabin will feel roomy?</h3>
          <p class="text-stone-600 text-sm">No. Capacity labels are not comfort measurements. Compare the interior dimensions with the users and seating position you expect before ordering.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-stone-900 text-white rounded-lg p-6 md:p-8 mt-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Need more room or traditional heat?</h2>
      <p class="text-stone-300 mb-5 max-w-2xl">Raise the product cap carefully, then compare the installation total. The next guide covers current options below $5,000 without pretending the sticker price is the whole project.</p>
      <a href="/guides/best-saunas-under-5000/" class="inline-flex min-h-12 items-center justify-center bg-amber-400 hover:bg-amber-500 text-stone-900 font-semibold px-6 py-3 rounded-md transition-colors">
        Compare the next budget tier
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
